    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it isnt just about being tired. it feels like there is no point to any of it. even when i stay clean for a bit, i just feel like i'm wasting time waiting for the next crash. like the end result is always the same regardless of how much work i put in. why keep pushing when the finish line doesnt even exist?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the finish line feels nonexistent, it's natural to question the point of the journey itself. Often, the goal of recovery shifts from achieving a permanent end to creating sustainable, manageable moments of peace. These small victories—a sober hour, a moment of calm—are powerful evidence that change is possible, even if the whole picture feels overwhelming right now. Focus on what you can build and protect in the present, rather than what you fear in the future.",
      "source": "target",
